 "title": "Mean and median of a geometric Brownian motion",
 "caption": "With μ = 8% and σ = 20%, the expected price grows as 100e^{0.08t} but the median as 100e^{0.06t}, because the volatility drag σ²/2 = 2% pulls the typical path below the mean. After one year: £108.33 against £106.18.",
 "alt": "Two exponential curves from £100: the mean rising faster than the median, 108.33 and 106.18 at one year.",
